{
  "description": "Deterministic resolution vectors for selection-dependent price_adjustments on binding fixed-price pricing options. Each resolution case names a declared option and the buyer's concrete selections (format_option_refs and placement refs, as they appear on the purchase), and asserts the resolved fixed_price and the ordered rows that fire. Rules under test: matching is full-identity equality across encodings; per dimension at most one row fires (the first matching row in declared order); firing rows apply in declared array order to a running total that starts at the option's fixed_price; rate rows apply to the running total at that position; after each row the total is rounded half away from zero to the option's price precision (the greater of the currency minor-unit precision and the most decimal places among fixed_price and row amounts) and never falls below zero. Arithmetic MUST be exact decimal or integer; binary floating point fails the rounding vectors.",
  "currency_minor_unit_exponent": {
    "USD": 2,
    "JPY": 0
  },
